Recreation* and a *Food*, it should only have been a *Recreation*. There was a specific entry on the Montlake Bridge that I kept as a *Feature*. I didn't know what grouping to put it in, but I think leaving it as a solo entry for **Type** was a mistake. It probably should have gone in *School*, which would have freed up space.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"uU1uwbFSNJyC"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Nevertheless, this TreeMap does have a strengths. While the text didn't turn out brilliantly, each layer and box can be expanded, so there shouldn't be any troubling reading the text itself. The grouping has issues, but still gives a good high-level idea of the different locations. It provides some indication of where our character(s) were spending their time in Seattle.\n","\n","There were many entries about gyms in Seattle (especially the IMA, though technically it's more than just a gym). So our character is an active individual who takes personal health seriously.\n","\n","There are several **Type**s of *School*-related entries, so they are making the most of their time on campus. They enjoy different *Scenic* spots on campus and their walks between classes.\n","\n","But most of their time seems to be spent off of the main UW campus, either at the IMA or in the rest of Seattle. They enjoy their time in open greenspace parks and gardens. They have found many different types of stores and businesses to check out and spend time in, everything from restaurants to groceries to game stores. They've even gone to see a chiropracter after spending all quarter stooping in their chair late into the night finishing off assignments. And of course, they've made a few notes about their dorms/apartments where they live while at UW."],"metadata":{"id":"fNTJ43dPSWMJ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Polar Bar Chart"],"metadata":{"id":"ZFKw1yDusf2f"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["I was a little disappointed in the TreeMap at first, so I decided to create a second visual. I liked the Polar Bar Chart."],"metadata":{"id":"e_Lvqrq9SaIV"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Once again, the size scalar is the number of words for each entry. The Polar Bar Chart maps out the different **SpecType**s from the data, with entries for each stacked on top of each other. Every **SpecType** has an entry on the chart, although some of them are very difficult to pinpoint with the cursor. Each entry can be hovered over to show the story and (precise) location for each entry."],"metadata":{"id":"My7U9W3VSnDG"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import plotly.express as px\n","\n","fig = px.bar_polar(df_treemap, r=\"totalwords2\", theta=\"SpecType\", color=\"totalwords2\", template=\"plotly_dark\",\n","            color_discrete_sequence= px.colors.sequential.Plasma_r, hover_data=['CleanBodyWrap', 'Location'])\n","fig.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":542},"id":"CFlCoBBisfYR","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1773032894068,"user_tz":420,"elapsed":238,"user":{"displayName":"Johann David Ravindranathan","userId":"10687580393656987052"}},"outputId":"f9aa5658-9f80-4f42-ef50-37bcc5c79c3c"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/html":["<html>\n","<head><meta charset=\"utf-8\" /></head>\n","<body>\n","    <div>            <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/mathjax/2.7.5/MathJax.js?config=TeX-AMS-MML_SVG\"></script><script type=\"text/javascript\">if (window.MathJax && window.MathJax.Hub && window.MathJax.Hub.Config) {window.MathJax.Hub.Config({SVG: {font: \"STIX-Web\"}});}</script>                <script type=\"text/javascript\">window.PlotlyConfig = {MathJaxConfig: 'local'};</script>\n","        <script charset=\"utf-8\" src=\"https://cdn.plot.ly/plotly-2.35.2.min.js\"></script>                <div id=\"1b6a026b-6d11-43d7-98bb-4759dada17cb\" class=\"plotly-graph-div\" style=\"height:525px; width:100%;\"></div>            <script type=\"text/javascript\">   